---
import ProductLayout from '../../../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';
---

<ProductLayout title="ST1200 Wide-Area Ionizing Air Blower | 140 × 120 cm Coverage | Shidike"
  description="ST1200 wide-area ionizing air blower. 150–360 CFM over a 140 × 120 cm area, ion balance 0 V ±10 V, 1280 mm long, 40–80 W — spans a full line rather than a single station."
  image="/assets/img/static-eliminator/st-1200.jpg">
  <section class="product-detail-page">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span>
        <a href="/products/static-eliminator">Static Eliminators &amp; Ionizing Bars</a><span>/</span>
        <span>ST1200</span>
      </div>

      <div class="product-top">
        <div class="product-gallery">
          <div class="product-main-image slider-wrapper">
            <button class="slider-arrow left" id="prevImage">&lsaquo;</button>
            <picture><source srcset="/assets/img/static-eliminator/st-1200.webp" type="image/webp" /><img
              id="mainProductImage"
              src="/assets/img/static-eliminator/st-1200.jpg"
              alt="ST1200 Horizontal Ion Fan"
            /></picture>
            <button class="slider-arrow right" id="nextImage">&rsaquo;</button>
          </div>
          <div class="product-thumbs">
            <picture><source srcset="/assets/img/static-eliminator/st-1200.webp" type="image/webp" /><img
              class="thumb-image active-thumb"
              src="/assets/img/static-eliminator/st-1200.jpg"
              alt="ST1200 thumbnail"
              data-full="/assets/img/static-eliminator/st-1200.jpg"
            /></picture>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="product-summary">
          <h1>ST1200 Horizontal Ion Fan</h1>
          <p class="product-short-desc">The widest coverage in the range: 140 × 120 cm at 150 to 360 CFM. At 1280 mm long the ST1200 spans a full production line rather than a single station, drawing 40 to 80 W depending on the fan setting.</p>

          <div class="product-actions">
            <button class="quote-btn" type="button">Get a Quote</button>
            <a href="https://wa.me/61436605126" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="whatsapp-btn">WhatsApp</a>
          </div>

          <dl class="key-specs">
            <div><dt>Air coverage</dt><dd><strong>140 × 120 cm</strong></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Airflow</dt><dd><strong>150–360 CFM</strong>, adjustable</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Ion balance</dt><dd><strong>0 V ±10 V</strong></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Length / weight</dt><dd><strong>1280 mm</strong> · 14.5 kg</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Power</dt><dd>40–80 W</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="key-specs-note">The widest coverage in the range. For a single bench position the ST101A or ST104A is the sensible size.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="detail-block pd-section">
        <h2>What the ST1200 Fixes</h2>
        <p class="pd-lede">If any of these is happening at your workstation, the cause is usually a surface charge nobody is measuring.</p>
        <ul class="fix-list">
          <li>
            <h3>The line is wider than any bench blower</h3>
            <p>A desktop unit covers 40 × 60 cm and a horizontal unit 60 × 120 cm. At 1280 mm long, the ST1200 covers 140 × 120 cm — a full line width rather than a station.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>Several blowers are being used to cover one area</h3>
            <p>Two or three units mounted in a row leave gaps between their coverage and multiply the wiring, the mounting and the maintenance. One wide unit does not.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <h3>The material charges faster than the air can reach it</h3>
            <p>At 150 to 360 CFM the ST1200 moves considerably more air than a bench unit, which is what carries ions to material that recharges continuously.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-block pd-section">
        <h2>How It Works</h2>
        <p>Corona discharge produces positive and negative ions along the full 1280 mm length, and the fan carries them across a 140 × 120 cm area. Airflow adjusts from 150 to 360 CFM, drawing 40 to 80 W, with ion balance held at 0 V ±10 V.</p>
        <p>
          The process is self-limiting: once a surface reaches neutral it stops taking up ions. What decides
          whether it works in practice is whether the airflow actually reaches the charged surface &mdash; which
          is why coverage area, not ion output, is the figure to size a blower on. Verify the result with a
          static field meter rather than assuming it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-block pd-section">
        <h2>Specifications</h2>
        <div class="spec-table-wrap">
          <table class="spec-table">
            <tr><td>Model</td><td>ST1200</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Operating voltage</td><td>110 V / 60 Hz or 220 V / 50 Hz</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Power</td><td>40 W to 80 W</td></tr>
            <tr><td>High-voltage generator</td><td>Built in</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Air volume</td><td>150–360 CFM, adjustable</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Air coverage</td><td>140 cm × 120 cm</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Ion balance</td><td>0 V ±10 V</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Operating temperature</td><td>−10 °C to 50 °C</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Dimensions</td><td>1280 mm (L) × 215 mm (W) × 190 mm (H)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Mounting</td><td>Suspended overhead or laid flat on a bench</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Weight</td><td>14.5 kg</td></tr>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-block pd-section">
        <h2>Decay Time &mdash; Measured</h2>
        <p>Measured decay times at three positions along the 1280 mm body, for both positive and negative charge. Even at the ends of a unit this long, decay stays within about 0.4 seconds of the centre at 900 mm.</p>
        <div class="spec-table-wrap">
          <table class="decay-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Position</th><th>300 mm</th><th>600 mm</th><th>900 mm</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Left, positive</td><td>0.9 s</td><td>2.1 s</td><td>2.9 s</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Left, negative</td><td>1.1 s</td><td>2.1 s</td><td>3.3 s</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Centre, positive</td><td>0.9 s</td><td>1.6 s</td><td>2.0 s</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Centre, negative</td><td>1.1 s</td><td>1.9 s</td><td>2.5 s</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Right, positive</td><td>0.9 s</td><td>1.8 s</td><td>2.5 s</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Right, negative</td><td>1.1 s</td><td>2.1 s</td><td>2.9 s</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="decay-note">Charge decay measured from 1 kV to 100 V, unit running on 110/220 V, ambient 22 &deg;C.</p>
        <p>Negative charge consistently takes slightly longer to clear than positive — about 0.2 seconds at 300 mm, widening to roughly 0.5 seconds at 900 mm. Size the mounting height on the slower of the two figures, not the faster.</p>
      </section>


      <div class="pd-mid-cta">
        <p>
          <strong>Not sure the ST1200 is the right size?</strong>
          Send the area you need to cover, what the material is and the measured surface voltage &mdash;
          we will come back with a model and a mounting position.
        </p>
        <button class="quote-btn" type="button">Ask an Engineer</button>
      </div>

      <section class="detail-block pd-section">
        <h2>Where It Goes</h2>
        <p class="pd-lede">A blower neutralizes an area rather than a line. At 1280 mm the ST1200 can be suspended over the work or laid flat on the bench. These are the positions it is sized for.</p>
        <div class="scenario-list">
          <div class="scenario-item">
            <h3>Full-width production lines</h3>
            <p>Where the charged area is a line rather than a station, and several bench units would leave gaps.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="scenario-item">
            <h3>Optical film and display panels</h3>
            <p>Large-format material where a single particle is a visible defect and the whole surface has to be neutral.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="scenario-item">
            <h3>Industrial packing stations</h3>
            <p>Wide packing and palletising areas where charged film and board attract contamination.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-block pd-section">
        <h2>Bar or Blower, and Which Blower</h2>
        <p>
          Use an <a href="/products/static-eliminator">ionizing bar</a> when the material moves past a fixed
          point &mdash; off a roller, out of a tool, off a stack. A bar mounted at that point neutralizes faster
          and holds a tighter balance, and is cut to the exact width of the material. Use a blower when the
          charge sits on a fixed area, or when there is no way to mount a bar within its 1 m working range.
        </p>
        <p>
          Between the blowers it is a question of area:
          <a href="/products/static-eliminator/st-s200">ST-S200</a> 450 &times; 450 mm to build into a machine,
          <a href="/products/static-eliminator/st-101a">ST101A</a> 40 &times; 60 cm for one position,
          <a href="/products/static-eliminator/st-104a">ST104A</a> 60 &times; 120 cm for a wider bench, and
          <a href="/products/static-eliminator/st-1200">ST1200</a> 140 &times; 120 cm across a full line.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-block faq-block pd-section">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary><h3 class="faq-question">What area does the ST1200 cover?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-answer">140 × 120 cm — the widest in the range, sized for a full line rather than a single station.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary><h3 class="faq-question">How much airflow does it deliver?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-answer">150 to 360 CFM, adjustable, drawing 40 to 80 W.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary><h3 class="faq-question">What ion balance does it hold?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-answer">0 V ±10 V.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary><h3 class="faq-question">How long is the unit?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-answer">1280 mm, weighing 14.5 kg — it is mounted over the line rather than stood on a bench.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary><h3 class="faq-question">What power supply does it need?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-answer">110 V / 60 Hz or 220 V / 50 Hz.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary><h3 class="faq-question">Should I use the ST1200 or ionizing bars?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-answer">If the material moves past a fixed point — off a roller, out of a tool, off a stack — bars mounted at that point will be faster and tighter, and can be cut to the exact width. The ST1200 is for a wide area that has to be neutralized as a whole, or where bars cannot be mounted close enough.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary><h3 class="faq-question">ST101A, ST104A or ST1200?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-answer">The ST101A covers 40 × 60 cm for one position, the ST104A 60 × 120 cm for a wider bench or two operators, and the ST1200 140 × 120 cm across a full line.</p>
          </details>
                  <details class="faq-item">
            <summary><h3 class="faq-question">How fast does the ST1200 neutralize?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-answer">At the centre, 1 kV falls to 100 V in about 0.9 seconds at 300 mm, 1.6 seconds at 600 mm and 2.0 seconds at 900 mm for positive charge, tested at 22 °C. At the ends of the 1280 mm body the same measurement takes about 2.9 seconds at 900 mm.</p>
          </details>
</div>
        <div class="pd-mid-cta" style="margin-top:30px;">
          <p>
            <strong>Request a quote for the ST1200</strong>
            Give us the area to cover, the material and the measured surface voltage.
          </p>
          <button class="quote-btn" type="button">Request a Quote</button>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-block pd-section">
        <h2>Related Products</h2>
        <div class="related-grid">
          <a href="/products/static-eliminator/st-101a" class="related-item">
            <picture><source srcset="/assets/img/static-eliminator/st-101a.webp" type="image/webp" /><img src="/assets/img/static-eliminator/st-101a.jpg" alt="ST101A Desktop Ionizing Air Blower" loading="lazy" /></picture>
